---
import Policy from '../layouts/Policy.astro';
import { contact } from '../data/site.js';

const updated = 'October 22, 2026';
const ga4 = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GA4_ID);
const pixel = Boolean(import.meta.env.PUBLIC_META_PIXEL_ID);
const tools = [ga4 && 'Google Analytics', pixel && 'the Meta Pixel'].filter(Boolean).join(' and ');
---
<Policy
  title="Privacy Policy | GENCI"
  description="How GENCI collects, uses and protects the information you send through the form, by phone, text or email, and the ad account data we access on Lead Engine."
  heading="Privacy policy"
  updated={updated}
>
  <section>
    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      GENCI edits short videos and runs Facebook and Instagram ads for home service businesses in the
      {contact.areaServed}. Questions about this policy go to <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a> or
      <a class="nobr" href={contact.tel}>{contact.phoneDisplay}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>
      When you fill out the form on our site, we receive your name, your type of business, your mobile number, your
      email and the plan you’re interested in. If you answer them, we also receive whether you run ads now and your
      monthly ad budget, plus a link to your footage if you add one. When you call, text or email us, we receive what
      you send.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use your information to reply about your request and our services, by text, email or phone, to recommend a
      plan and an ad budget that fit your business, and to deliver the videos you order. If you would rather not get
      texts, tell us and we will stop.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Ad account data on Lead Engine</h2>
    <p>
      On the Lead Engine plan, you give GENCI partner access to your Facebook and Instagram ad account. Through that
      access we see how your campaigns perform, such as spend, reach, clicks and cost per result, and the leads your
      ads generate.
    </p>
    <p>
      We use this data only to manage and improve your campaigns and to prepare your monthly report. We do not sell it
      or share it with third parties. When you cancel or remove our access, we stop using your account.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who handles it</h2>
    <p>
      Form submissions reach us through Formspree, a form service. Our website host keeps basic server logs, such as IP
      address and browser type, to run and secure the site. We do not sell or rent your personal information.
    </p>
    {tools ? (
      <p>
        We use {tools} to count visits and measure the results of our ads. These tools set cookies and receive data
        such as the pages you view, your device type and whether you sent the form. You can block them in your browser
        settings. This site does not respond to browser Do Not Track signals.
      </p>
    ) : (
      <p>This site does not use cookies for advertising or analytics.</p>
    )}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
    <p>
      We keep your information for as long as we need it to reply to you and work with you. To see, correct or delete
      what we have, email <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>California residents</h2>
    <p>
      You can ask what personal information we have about you and ask us to delete it. We do not sell or share personal
      information as those terms are defined under California law.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>This site is for business owners. We do not knowingly collect information from children under 13.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>When this policy changes, we will post the new version on this page with a new date.</p>
  </section>
</Policy>
